# Nayak Database Migrations

This directory contains the Alembic migrations for the Nayak backend. The
application uses SQLAlchemy models and Supabase PostgreSQL as the database.

## Configuration

Set the Supabase SQLAlchemy connection string in the backend `.env` file:

```env
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE
```

Alembic loads this value through `alembic/env.py` and uses
`Base.metadata` from `app.models.models` to compare the models with the
database schema.

## Apply Migrations

Run these commands from the backend directory:

```bash
uv run alembic upgrade head
```

This applies all migrations that have not yet been applied to Supabase.

## After a Schema Change

Whenever a SQLAlchemy model or database schema changes:

```bash
uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the schema change"
uv run alembic upgrade head
```

Always inspect the generated file in `alembic/versions/` before applying it.
Do not use `Base.metadata.create_all()` to update an existing schema.

## Existing Database

If the tables already exist in Supabase and match the models, mark the current
migration as applied without executing it:

```bash
uv run alembic stamp head
```

Use `stamp` only when the existing database has already been checked. It does
not create or modify tables.